cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
title: "Analysis code for a non-inferiority and multivariable logistic regression analysis of functional outcome in oldest-old convalescent rehabilitation inpatients"
abstract: >-
  R code implementing preprocessing, cohort description, Brunner-Munzel
  non-inferiority testing of motor FIM gain with Hodges-Lehmann shifts and
  ATS interaction tests, and a multivariable logistic regression of good
  functional outcome using restricted cubic splines and
  substantive-model-compatible multiple imputation (smcfcs), including
  separation handling, variable and interaction selection, performance
  assessment and bootstrap optimism correction. No individual patient data
  are included.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yoneda
    given-names: Yuto
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-0338-5673"
license: MIT
